# Figma Make → Choremaxx Sync

## Source of truth

- Design visual/layout source: Figma Make  
  https://www.figma.com/make/4J6d4LW335tDyEDpqq3VD1/Design-Orbit-AI-App
- Product brand (Make v7+): **Choremaxx** (shipping product name). Internal code namespaces may still say `orbit` for stability.
- Product/IA source of truth for shipping product remains `docs/product-context.md`, `docs/ux-design-system.md`, and `docs/technical-blueprint.md`.
- Saved Make mirror + sync metadata: `design/make/` (`SYNC_STATE.json`, `source/`).
- Automation prompt for Cursor Automations / Cloud Agents: `docs/figma-sync-automation.md`.

## Current Make navigation (v7)

Primary tabs in Make: **Home, Tasks, Plan, Rewards, Nova**.  
Plan = Calendar + Itineraries. Rewards = Rewards + Allowance + Rankings.  
Role filters: child hides Plan; roommate hides Rewards.  
Settings/Admin and Create Task are overlays — not tabs.  
Groceries remain in-app (Home / Settings / deep link) but are not a primary tab in v7.

## Sync workflow (only when explicitly requested)

**Do not sync or port Make on your own.** Starting Metro/tunnel, fixing a bug, or
continuing chat is **not** permission to re-port Make or switch to a Make-v7 branch.
Only sync when the user pastes a Make URL or clearly says to sync/port from Figma.

Figma does not push live into Expo by itself. Changes are registered via the
design registry and applied by a Cursor agent (manual trigger, schedule, or
Automation):

1. User pastes the Make URL, says “sync from Figma”, or Automation runs.
2. Agent calls Figma MCP `get_design_context` with `fileKey=4J6d4LW335tDyEDpqq3VD1` and `nodeId=0:1`.
3. Agent fetches Make source via MCP resources (`file://figma/make/source/4J6d4LW335tDyEDpqq3VD1/...`) into `design/make/source/` and updates `design/make/SYNC_STATE.json`.
4. Agent ports UI into Expo Router / React Native under `app/` and `components/orbit/`, using tokens in `constants/orbit-theme.ts` — do not paste Tailwind/web DOM code directly.
5. **Backend wire-up:** if the design introduces entities or fields, extend `supabase/` schema, repository supabase paths, and `store/orbit-store.tsx`. Do not leave new screens hard-coded mock-only when `EXPO_PUBLIC_DATA_MODE=supabase`.
6. Open a PR; user verifies in Expo Go (`npx expo start`) and staging supabase.

## Porting rules

- Map web Make screens to native: View/Text/Pressable/ScrollView, existing GlassCard / StatusPill / OrbitButton / ChoremaxxLogo where possible.
- Mock mode (`store/orbit-store.tsx`, `data/mock-household.ts`) remains for Expo Go design testing; supabase mode must work for shipping builds.
- Rewards Center lives on `app/(tabs)/rewards.tsx` (tab title **Rewards**).
- Plan lives on `app/(tabs)/calendar.tsx` (tab title **Plan**).
- Onboarding: `app/onboarding.tsx` (role + motivation) before auth signup.
